      "title": "Historic US ocean liner sinks near Florida to become world’s largest artificial reef",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/11/ss-united-states-sinks-florida-reef",
      "description": "<p>SS United States, which set transatlantic speed record during maiden voyage in 1952, is sunk off coast of Destin</p><p>The historic SS United States has reached the end of its journey at sea, sinking Wednesday off the coast of Destin, Florida, where it will begin a new life underwater as an artificial reef.</p><p>The nearly 1,000ft American-made vessel, once the fastest ocean liner in the world, was launched in 1952 and made history by setting a transatlantic speed record during its maiden voyage. The ship carried thousands of passengers across the Atlantic over 17 years of operation before being retired in 1969.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/11/ss-united-states-sinks-florida-reef\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-12T03:07:16"
    }
